# IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS: cu-003 (writer: CU folders + SYNOPSIS.itr)
# TIMESTAMP: 2026-10-09
# WORKDIR: itr-compiler/
# DEPENDS_ON: cu-001 merged (uses CU.componentFileNames, CUBatch.synopsis)

STEP 1 — Write per-CU component files.
File: src/main/scala/itrcompiler/infrastructure/filesystem/FileSystem.scala
- In `write`, FIRST branch: if `cu.cuType == RegularCU && cu.components.nonEmpty`,
  write ONLY the cu-<id>/ component files via `writeComponents` and RETURN —
  no per-CU .itr blob is ever written for such CUs. Component-less CUs
  (legacy batches) keep the existing path: one <cu-id>.itr frame inside
  cu-<id>/, never at the output root.
- Create directory `outFolder.resolve(cu.id)`; for each `(key, body)` in
  `cu.components`, write file `CU.componentFileNames(key)` with content:
  `"# " + key.toUpperCase.replace("-", "_") + ": " + cu.id + "\n\n" + body + "\n"`
  (yields `# COORDINATES: cu-001`, matching the manual ITR layout).
- Component files obey the SAME `force` flag as the flat frame: skip when
  the file exists and `force=false` (mirrors the existing early-return, so
  manual folders survive recompiles).
- Never delete any file in the output folder. Only create or overwrite the
  exact paths above. Advisor-placed overrides are therefore preserved by
  construction.

STEP 2 — Write root SYNOPSIS.itr once per compile.
- Add method to FileSystem:
```scala
def writeSynopsis(outFolder: Path, synopsis: CUSynopsis, cus: Seq[CU], force: Boolean): Unit = {
  Files.createDirectories(outFolder)
  val target = outFolder.resolve("SYNOPSIS.itr")
  if (!force && Files.exists(target)) return
  val body =
    s"FEATURES_IMPLEMENTED=${synopsis.features.mkString(",")}\n" +
    s"MAX_ATTEMPTS=${synopsis.maxAttempts}\n" +
    s"CUS=${cus.map(_.id).mkString(",")}\n" +
    s"ENFORCED_BY=itr-compiler\n" +
    s"SUMMARY=${synopsis.summary}\n"
  Files.write(target, body.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8))
}
```
- File: src/main/scala/itrcompiler/application/services/Compile.scala — call
  `cuStore`/`fileSystem.writeSynopsis` after the per-CU store loop, only
  when `batch.synopsis.isDefined`. (Validation in cu-002 guarantees it is
  defined in batch mode; single-CU raw mode has no synopsis -> skip.)
- Wiring: FileSystem already implements all ports; expose writeSynopsis
  through CUStore (`def storeSynopsis(...)`) to keep Compile depending on
  the application layer, not infrastructure directly (ARCH.DIP).

